{%- comment -%}
  Grid-only, LAYOUT-LESS view of a collection.

  Used by assets/pm-pagesize.js (TC-088 in-stock-first stitch + TC-091 virtual
  pagination) as a fast data source: it fetches
    /collections/<handle>?<active filters>&view=grid&page=N
  to grab product cards WITHOUT re-rendering the whole theme (header, mega-menu,
  facets, footer, every script) the way a full-page fetch does. `{% layout none %}`
  ships only the <ul> below — a fraction of the bytes and server render time — so
  the in-stock-first re-order completes much faster.

  Shopify applies the URL's availability filter + sort to collection.products here
  exactly as on the real page, so the in-stock / quote views come out correct.
  Must mirror the grid contract pm-pagesize.js reads: ul.pm-plp__grid with
  data-pm-total (the filtered count) + data-pm-server-size, and one <li> per card.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- layout none -%}
{%- paginate collection.products by 24 -%}
<ul class="pm-plp__grid" data-pm-view-mode="grid" data-pm-total="{{ paginate.items }}" data-pm-server-size="24">
  {%- for product in collection.products -%}
    <li>{%- render 'pm-product-card', product: product -%}</li>
  {%- endfor -%}
</ul>
{%- endpaginate -%}
